{"content":"I now have the complete picture. Let me provide the answer.\n\nh06.\n\n**Handlers (6 total, all on `APIV1Service`):**\n\n| # | RPC Handler | File | Webhook activity |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `CreateMemo` | `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:70` | `memos.memo.created` |\n| 2 | `UpdateMemo` | `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:401` | `memos.memo.updated` |\n| 3 | `DeleteMemo` | `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:518` | `memos.memo.deleted` |\n| 4 | `CreateMemoComment` | `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_comments.go:20` | `memos.memo.comment.created` (+ `memos.memo.created` via inner `CreateMemo` call) |\n| 5 | `SetMemoAttachments` | `server/router/api/v1/memo_attachment_service.go:16` | `memos.memo.updated` |\n| 6 | `SetMemoRelations` | `server/router/api/v1/memo_relation_service.go:16` | `memos.memo.updated` |\n\n**Convergence function:** `dispatchMemoRelatedWebhook` — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_webhooks.go:48`\n\nAll six paths funnel through this single private method (the \"comment created\" path from `CreateMemoComment` has an additional direct call to `DispatchMemoCommentCreatedWebhook` that bypasses `dispatchMemoRelatedWebhook`, but its *other* leg through `CreateMemo` still converges there). The three thin public wrappers — `DispatchMemoCreatedWebhook` (:15), `DispatchMemoUpdatedWebhook` (:20), and `DispatchMemoDeletedWebhook` (:25) — are one-liners that immediately delegate to `dispatchMemoRelatedWebhook`.\n\nInside `dispatchMemoRelatedWebhook`, the user's configured webhooks are fetched via `s.Store.GetUserWebhooks`, each webhook's URL is set on the payload, and delivery is handed off to `webhook.PostAsync` (`internal/webhook/webhook.go:184`), which enqueues to a bounded async channel. Worker goroutines (spawned in `init()` at `:42`) drain that channel and call `webhook.Post` (`:120`), which performs the actual outbound `HTTP POST` to the user-configured URL using `safeClient`.","iteration":11,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
